# Tuna Melts

{ rating="4" image="tuna_melts.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 cans (5 oz each) [Tuna]{ ing="tuna" }, drained
- [ ] 2-3 Tbsp [Mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }
- [ ] 2-3 Tbsp [chopped Dill Pickle]{ ing="chopped-dill-pickle" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Lemon Juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] [Salt and Black Pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" } to taste
- [ ] 4-5 [English Muffins]{ ing="english-muffins" }, split
- [ ] 8-10 slices [Cheese]{ ing="cheese" } (Muenster, Provolone, Havarti, Pepper Jack, Swiss, Cheddar, etc.)

### Optional additions for flavor/health

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [finely diced Celery]{ ing="finely-diced-celery" } (adds crunch)
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [finely diced Red Onion]{ ing="finely-diced-red-onion" } or 1/2 tsp Onion Powder
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Garlic Powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Dijon Mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [Greek Yogurt]{ ing="greek-yogurt" } (can replace half the mayo for lighter version)
- [ ] Fresh [Dill or Parsley]{ ing="dill-or-parsley" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to Broil (~10 min)
1. In a bowl, combine drained [tuna]{ ing="tuna" }, [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }, chopped [pickle]{ ing="chopped-dill-pickle" }, [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, salt, and [pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" }. Add any optional ingredients if using. Mix well
1. Toast [English muffin]{ ing="english-muffins" } halves until lightly golden
1. On a foil-lined baking sheet, spread tuna mixture on each muffin half, top with [cheese]{ ing="cheese" } slice
1. Broil for 2-3 minutes until cheese is melted and bubbly

## Notes

1. Can be made in a pinch by toasting the English muffins, then topping them and steaming them in a hot pan with a lid
